# QUATA Digital — QCP WhatsApp template reconciliation cron template.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# QCP's template rows carry Meta's category, and Meta re-classifies templates
# on its own schedule. A template that was AUTHENTICATION when it was approved
# can become MARKETING underneath us — and a *marketing* template carrying a
# login code is the exact condition that gets a number restricted. If that
# number is Quata Verify, QuataFood's login OTP, payment-PIN reset and
# phone-change verification all stop, and none of the three has an email
# fallback: the user is locked out of the account entirely.
#
# Nothing noticed that on its own. The reconciliation existed but only ran
# when an operator opened the console and pressed Sync.
#
# WHAT IT DOES
#
# POST /api/v1/admin/qcp/templates/sync-due reconciles every *live* account
# that has not been reconciled within the interval (default 3600s), deciding
# due-ness from the existing `template.sync` audit row. It is:
#
#   * idempotent — safe at any frequency; a call that finds nothing due is a
#     single audit read and returns `{"due": 0}`;
#   * dormant-safe — only accounts with `is_active` AND a stored access token
#     are considered, so a fresh install dials Meta zero times;
#   * incapable of enabling anything — it cannot activate an account, enable a
#     product or start delivery. The only status it writes is the `disabled`
#     of a template quarantine.
#
# It is deliberately NOT gated on the delivery master switch: catching a
# re-classification matters most while sending is paused.
#
# The QCP worker (`python -m app.scripts.whatsapp_worker`) calls the same
# function every 60 cycles. Either alone is enough; running both costs one
# extra audit read per hour. Install this if the worker is not deployed, or as
# a belt if it is.
#
# PERMISSION
#
# The endpoint is gated on `settings:manage` — NOT on `whatsapp:operate`, and
# that is deliberate: reconciling with Meta reads and quarantines, it never
# switches a number on. Issue a long-lived service token from /admin/staff for
# a dedicated cron user holding `settings:manage` and nothing else.
#
# Install:
#   sudo crontab -e
#   # then paste the line below, replacing $ADMIN_TOKEN with that token.
#
# */15 * * * *  curl -fsS -X POST https://api.quatadigital.com/api/v1/admin/qcp/templates/sync-due \
#                    -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADMIN_TOKEN" \
#                    >> /var/log/quata-qcp-template-sync.log 2>&1
